    "content": "The Faithful: Women of the Bible is a 2026 Fox three-week limited series (premiering March 22, 2026) focusing on the lives of Sarah, Hagar, Rebekah, Leah, and Rachel. Starring Minnie Driver as Sarah, this 6-episode drama portrays the faith, struggles, and, in the case of the sisters Leah and Rachel, rivalries of the women in Genesis. Key Details About the Series: Premiere Date: Sunday, March 22, 2026, at 8 p.m. ET/PT on FOX, concluding on Easter Sunday, April 5. Characters/Cast: Minnie Driver (Sarah), Natacha Karam (Hagar), Alexa Davalos (Rebekah), Blu Hunt (Rachel), and Jeffrey Donovan (Abraham). Focus: The series highlights the emotional, personal, and spiritual journeys of these women and their impact on the foundational stories of the Old Testament. Streaming: Episodes are available on Hulu the day after their airing, notes this Tom's Guide article. Biblical Women Featured: Sarah: Wife of Abraham, navigating a long wait for a child. Hagar: Former slave to Sarah, whose life is irrevocably linked to the family's path. Rebekah: Known for securing the destiny of her preferred child. Leah & Rachel: Sisters and co-wives whose sibling rivalry shapes early Israelite history. The show was produced by Fox Entertainment Studios and filmed in Italy.",
